heck-outs.","r":""},{"s":22.29,"e":28.19,"t":"Uh, Doug will get a chance to do some flying, actually, of the vehicle close to the International Space Station, for example.","r":""},{"s":28.19,"e":35.3,"t":"And we'll make sure all those systems are working for future missions that might not necessarily exercise all those different features of the vehicle.","r":""},{"s":38.1,"e":48.58,"t":"The fundamental purpose of the Demo-2 mission is to get certification for, uh, uh, future, uh, missions from, uh, SpaceX to the International Space Station rotating crew, uh,","r":""},{"s":48.58,"e":50.95,"t":"to meet NASA's needs aboard the Space Station.","r":""},{"s":54.19,"e":64.4,"t":"The SpaceX vehicle, uh, has a lot of features and capabilities that, uh, hopefully we never have to utilize in a real mission, uh, but Doug and I will make sure that they are all ready,","r":""},{"s":64.4,"e":65.86,"t":"just in case we do.","r":""},{"s":65.86,"e":75.01,"t":"And, uh, it's everything from, uh, a response to a fire on board, uh, to, uh, flying close to the, uh, International Space Station manually instead of letting the computer do it.","r":""},{"s":75.01,"e":83.25,"t":"We'll make sure all those systems are working, uh, during the test flight, so that the future missions, uh, will have 'em available, even if they don't plan to utilize 'em.","r":""},{"s":85.58,"e":93.09,"t":"Absolutely, we've got a lot of objectives, uh, onboard the, uh, vehicle that we need to accomplish to really make sure that it's, uh, good to go.","r":""},{"s":93.09,"e":101.73,"t":"Uh, we'll do everything from actually talk from the Dragon vehicle to a Russian Soyuz, uh, once we get a closer dock to the International Space Station,","r":""},{"s":101.73,"e":104.24,"t":"just to make sure that comm system was, uh, working.","r":""},{"s":104.24,"e":118.02,"t":"If you ever needed it to-- during an emergency, we'll, uh, take the spacesuits on and off in a couple of different, uh, situations to make sure that we have, uh, good data for how long that takes if you had to do it from an emergency response perspective.","r":""},{"s":118.02,"e":128.33,"t":"We'll dig out all kinds of hardware that's stowed in the, uh, nooks and crannies of the vehicle so that we have a-a good feel for how things are in place and, uh, getting them back in place, uh, prior to entry.","r":""},{"s":128.33,"e":140.44,"t":"And so we, uh, plan to do all those things as a-- just a part of our test mission, so missions in the future can focus on the real mission, which is getting trained crews to the International Space Station.","r":""},{"s":143.01,"e":148.41,"t":"You know, as we get, uh, closer and closer to the launch date, we've had to balance, uh, a lot of things.","r":""},{"s":148.41,"e":153.49,"t":"We've had to, uh, accept kind of the status of the vehicle and then, uh, understand how we're gonna operate it.","r":""},{"s":153.49,"e":160.56,"t":"And I think really both Doug and I's focus is making sure that, uh, we're proficient, uh, for whatever launch dates come.","r":""},{"s":160.56,"e":163.76,"t":"We've had the launch date kinda, uh, slip a little bit to this point.","r":""},{"s":163.76,"e":173.24,"t":"And so we're really chasing the final-final preparations to make sure that we're, uh, on time and on target for the launch date right now, which is, uh, in late May.","r":""},{"s":176.61,"e":181.55,"t":"You know, there's-- there are parts of it-- of the mission that are discovery, and there are parts of it that aren't, right?","r":""},{"s":181.55,"e":189.99,"t":"And so you just want to know which parts are in the discovery portion of things, which part is exploration, and which part your-- you know, in our case,","r":""},{"s":189.99,"e":193.06,"t":"we're-we're providing a vehicle to, uh, future crews.","r":""},{"s":193.06,"e":201.77,"t":"And so our intent is to make that vehicle predictable and-and I-- and figure out everything so that we can come back and tell them, so that the-the vehicle itself is predictable,","r":""},{"s":201.77,"e":204.67,"t":"even though the mission itself might not be, right?","r":""},{"s":204.67,"e":205.87,"t":"So, um...","r":""},{"s":205.87,"e":217.15,"t":"Maybe it's a complicated way to describe it, but, uh, you know, you want Dragon's vehicle response to be predictable, so that when we-- we can use that to discover things with the International Space Station.","r":""},{"s":217.15,"e":224.96,"t":"Our intent is to not, you know, try to, uh, explore the Mach envelope for a capsule coming through the atmosphere, necessarily.","r":""},{"s":224.96,"e":234.17,"t":"You know, and-and-and see whether or not that was, uh, a limit that, you know, human wise, we could tolerate or we couldn't tolerate sort of a thing.","r":""},{"s":234.17,"e":242.38,"t":"Our intent is to provide this vehicle to enable the-- the real exploration mission, which in this case is keeping the Space Station, uh, operating,","r":""},{"s":242.38,"e":251.75,"t":"keeping the scientific discoveries, uh, even the-the human piece of that with, uh-- with crew members on orbit for extended duration, keep that data continuing to come.","r":""},{"s":251.75,"e":253.75,"t":"That's what we're providing with this vehicle.","r":""},{"s":253.75,"e":261.79,"t":"Our-our goal is to-- is to-to-to not necessarily have every aspect of the-the vehicle's performance be an exploration objective,","r":""},{"s":261.79,"e":267.33,"t":"you know, 'cause we're focused on a different real exp-- exploration objective with the International Space Station.","r":""},{"s":270.14,"e":275.57,"t":"I think that the mission that we have in front of us and the-the success that we're gonna have is a representation of America.","r":""},{"s":275.57,"e":280.55,"t":"Um, bringing it back to the Florida coast is, uh, uh, a really, really cool thing.","r":""},{"s":280.55,"e":290.79,"t":"Just to see how many people from across the country have to pull together to pull something like this off is just a-- it's inspiring to me, and-and I'm just excited to be a part of it.","r":""}]}
